      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "Heightfield raises a picture into ground: each point stands at Base plus Height times the picture's brightness, painted by the picture itself. The picture is a Perlin Noise walking round its loop with the gear, so hills rise and sink, and a Ground chained on after it is a lake. Try Height and the noise's Scale; too low a Steepness tears the slopes, too high makes the march crawl."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
